<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Isabela</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1494">1494</a>–<a href="/years/1498">1498</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Isabela was the first Spanish town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a> on the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a>, in the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a>, during his second voyage at the start of 1494. Disease, hunger and quarrels plagued the settlers, and it was abandoned within a few years in favour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a>. Its remains are an archaeological park.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/la-isabela.jpg" alt="La Isabela" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heralder · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Banner_of_the_Crown_of_Castille_(Habsburg_Style).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
